{
    "$schema": "vendor/infection/infection/resources/schema.json",
    "source": {
        "directories": ["src"]
    },
    "logs": {
        "text": "php://stderr",
        "summary": "build/infection-summary.log"
    },
    "testFramework": "testo",
    // Achieved Covered Code MSI 96% (510/529 killed, 2026-08-22 after the
    // untrusted-cookie hardening). The floor stays at 96. The 17 remaining
    // escapees are true equivalents — verified one by one, not coverage gaps
    // (Infection also reported one errored and one timed-out mutant, neither
    // of which survived as normal behavior):
    //   - ReturnRemoval early-exits whose fall-through reaches the same return
    //     via the next guard (BodyUtmSource:47, DefaultLandingPageSanitizer:43
    //     and :78, HeaderUtmSource:69, UtmParameters:103).
    //   - CastInt in InMemoryUtmAttributionRepository:122 (two operands) — the
    //     id column is a numeric string, and PHP's <=> coerces operands, so
    //     dropping either cast yields the same ordering.
    //   - MBString on URL scheme (DefaultLandingPageSanitizer:52) — RFC schemes
    //     are ASCII-only, so mb_strtolower and strtolower agree.
    //   - BitwiseOr on ClickIds JSON flags (ClickIds:134) — the value pattern
    //     forbids '/', so UNESCAPED_SLASHES is a no-op on real input.
    //   - ConcatOperandRemoval in HeaderUtmSource:40 — UtmParameters::pick
    //     accepts the bare key as a fallback, so the campaign tuple is the same.
    //   - UnwrapArrayIntersectKey in QueryUtmSource:49 — UtmParameters ignores
    //     unrelated query keys, while click ids are filtered independently.
    //   - UnwrapArrayValues in UtmHistory:34 — `...$touchpoints` always yields
    //     a 0-indexed list, so array_values is a no-op.
    //   - ReturnRemoval in UtmCookieCodec:100 (the JsonException catch) — the
    //     fall-through hits the next guard, which rejects the undefined
    //     $decoded and returns the same empty history.
    //   - MBString on the referrer scheme (Referrer:60) — RFC 3986 schemes are
    //     ASCII-only, so mb_strtolower and strtolower agree. Same class as
    //     DefaultLandingPageSanitizer:52 above.
    //   - Continue_ -> break in UtmCaptureMiddleware::withinWindow (:143) —
    //     UtmHistory is sorted newest first, so every touchpoint after a stale
    //     one is older and therefore stale too. Skipping the rest and dropping
    //     the rest produce the identical kept list. The equivalence rests on
    //     that sort invariant, not on the loop.
    //   - NullSafePropertyCall (UtmCookieCodec:139, UtmFingerprint:33) — on PHP
    //     8.5, `null->property` emits E_WARNING and evaluates to null. Testo does
    //     not promote that warning to failure, so the observed value is equal.
    "minMsi": 96,
    "mutators": {
        "@default": true
    }
}
